{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547728-wonder-crafting-requirements","id":1547728,"title":"Wonder Crafting Requirements?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-14T01:26:37-08:00","id":1547728,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Wonder Crafting Requirements?","content":"I see a lot of mismatches throughout the books, I was hoping anyone would have a logical explanation...<br /> <br /> <b>HDYDT p. 46 specifies the following:</b><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/vjbCJ41.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>While BoS p.160 say otherwise...</b><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/wU1uTgI.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what exactly are <i>temporary</i> Talismans? Once you have infused the energy into an item, it's there to stay, and you don't really need to acquire more successes to extend the duration of the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T05:11:04-08:00","id":1547733,"title":"","content":"Use BoS. It's the book with the dedicated section, and it's more developped.<br /> <br /> *There are &quot;temporary&quot; Wonders, but they're not called Talismans: Charms/Gadgets can be created with Prime 3 and expire after use. HDYDT text it's either a &quot;typo&quot;, or introducing a new type of Wonder that was never talked about - since it ain't doing any effort to introduce the second option, I believe it must be a typo.<br /> <br /> *I don't remember if on M20 you can do this, but in previous editions it was possible to reduce the Prime level required to make a Wonder by one, if you were using Tass of an appropiate Ressonance to craft the item (i.e: tass with a destructive ressonance could lower the Prime required to craft a weapon Talisman to 3, instead of 4). Maybe that's why HDYDT says what it says.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T09:32:00-08:00","id":1547741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547728-wonder-crafting-requirements?p=1547733#post1547733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use BoS. It's the book with the dedicated section, and it's more developped.<br /> <br /> *There are &quot;temporary&quot; Wonders, but they're not called Talismans: Charms/Gadgets can be created with Prime 3 and expire after use. HDYDT text it's either a &quot;typo&quot;, or introducing a new type of Wonder that was never talked about - since it ain't doing any effort to introduce the second option, I believe it must be a typo.<br /> <br /> *I don't remember if on M20 you can do this, but in previous editions it was possible to reduce the Prime level required to make a Wonder by one, if you were using Tass of an appropiate Ressonance to craft the item (i.e: tass with a destructive ressonance could lower the Prime required to craft a weapon Talisman to 3, instead of 4). Maybe that's why HDYDT says what it says.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey there Aleph, and thank you for your time!<br /> So &quot;<i>temporary</i> Talismans&quot; do not only appear on HDYDT p.46, but they also appear on the third dot of Prime on the corebook:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9VW0ZIM.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, &quot;<i>temporary</i> Talismans&quot; classified as Charms is something that I thought of... until I looked one bullet above on the same section (HDYDT p.46), and they already had that listed.<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/JI38aR1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> After proving that &quot;<i>temporary</i> Talismans&quot; are not supposed to be Charms, I was trying to dig in the books and look for information about the matter. But there isn't any explanation on what that might be. Now since all Wonders are basically permanent, as they are infused with Quintessence, I find a bit hard to determine what &quot;temporary&quot; would mean.<br /> One approach I thought of, would be a Talisman that cannot have its Quintessence re-filled, and once it is running out, the magick has faded away...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T12:26:33-08:00","id":1547744,"title":"","content":"OK, looking at this more in-depth:<br /> <br /> *The Sphere says &quot;Temporary Wonders&quot;, then it goes on to say <i>temporary </i>Talismans. It doesn't explain what are these.<br /> There's no mention of Charms in levels 3 nor 2.<br /> Following the links to the Crafcting Wonders section, Talismans are on Prime 4, there's no mention of &quot;temporary Talimans&quot;, Charms are also absent.<br /> <br /> However, there's a Charm on M20: The Madness Grenade example on the toybox p. 662 it's obviously a Charm by it's rules and concept, but it's presented as a Talisman.<br /> <br /> Follwing trough the Toybox it says: <i>&quot;The following systems are, by necessity, brief and basic. for an expanded set of optional Wonder rules, <b>see The Book of Secrets</b>&quot;</i> (as per p. 631 of M20)<br /> <br /> *Let's go to <b>BoS</b>: There's no temporary Talismans, but Charms are mentioned, note that Prime 3 it's the Sphere Level you need to create Charms when you're not reducing the cost trough using Tass with the correct ressonance (<b>Simple Charm = </b>Prime 2 (appropriate energy),<b> Prime 3 (any energy)</b>, BoS p.160 - also the way it has been from previous editions)<br /> <br /> *HDYDT states Charms are made at Prime 2. But HDYDT isn't defining what each of these &quot;reserved words&quot; it's mentioning mean, you're supposed to know already. And the actual place where you're supposed to look for the rules, says it's 2 <i>only in the case you have the appropiate Tass</i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />...and now I've realized a player could look at HDYDT and expect to be able to make Charms with Prime 2 regardless of the energy used, but if you want to go with that you have to reject <i>the very book </i><i>where the word &quot;Charm&quot; it's defined as a thing on M20</i>, <i>that even HDYDT mentions as the place where you should look...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i><br /> <br /> However, note that HDYDT isn't presenting new systems, it's just listing what exists by name and telling you where to look. <hr /><br /> So, this is what I'm led to believe:<br /> <br /> *Charms were cut from M20, perhaps because the author didn't wanted to clog the book with more &quot;reserved words&quot;. Yet, the idea of making objects &quot;like&quot; Charms exists in M20, both because it's legacy, and it's also present in the book. Wonder rules are still being restored, but the concept of &quot;temporary wonder&quot; makes sense as something you would want to introduce from the get go.<br /> <br /> *BoS introduced Charms at their correct level, Prime 3 (with shenanigans to reduce it to 2). The concept of &quot;temporary wonder&quot; now reffers to this.<br /> <br /> *HDYDT it's sitting in an odd middle ground, it keept &quot;temporary Talimans&quot; at level 3 and introduced Charms w/o explaining what they are at 2 (HDYDT it's from 2015, BoS from 2017). Old players would know what those words mean, but new players would have to wait two years for BoS to know. Perhaps the authors didn't know yet if these &quot;temporary Talismans&quot; were going to exist as it's own thing yet. As things turned out, they're an empty variable<br /> <br /> Considering all of this: It doesn't seem likely to me that M20 wants to introduce a new type of wonder here. If they had wanted, they would just have done so like they did with with the Trinkets. Authors created the concept of Trinkets for M20, remembered about them in all their books, but then forgor twice to add a single mention or example of their also new concept of &quot;temporary Talismans&quot;? I guess it's not 100% impossible, but I think it's more likely it was a placeholder for Charms, and HDYDT just confused it's stuff. <hr /><br /> But temporary Talismans it's not a bad concept:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One approach I thought of, would be a Talisman that cannot have its Quintessence re-filled, and once it is running out, the magick has faded away... </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would rather re-skin Charms: You could use the Charm rules but instead of being a batch of X single use items, you make a single item with X uses. That way you don't have to invent new rules to create and value magic items, and get the exact same results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-15-2025, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T07:16:09-08:00","id":1547755,"title":"","content":"Of course there wasn't room for Charms, we desperately needed multiple specialized rules for making the Vampire Lawn Chair rote unusable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T07:25:18-08:00","id":1547758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547728-wonder-crafting-requirements?p=1547755#post1547755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course there wasn't room for Charms, we desperately needed multiple specialized rules for making the Vampire Lawn Chair rote unusable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! Priorities.<br /> <br /> I would advise to use forged by dragon fire rules. They seem far less confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T08:14:33-08:00","id":1547760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547728-wonder-crafting-requirements?p=1547744#post1547744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for the thorough explanation.<br /> It does make more sense now, I figured it'd require the knowledge of somebody who has a long-time MTA knowledge to figure it out...<br /> Yeah, MTA is extremely inconsistent, but I guess we gotta work with what we have...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-18T13:05:04-08:00","id":1547815,"title":"","content":"You know, I've always thought that the Charm rules should allow for items that aren't &quot;consumed&quot; in the sense we usually use it (potions, bullets, etc), but are rather persistent objects that just have a limited number of &quot;charges&quot;. Like a wand that shoots pure magical energy (Prime 3), but only a certain number of times.<br /> <br /> (This then leading to funny situations, where a family line's &quot;Unique Focus&quot; is a magic wand passed down from an ancestor who received it from their Awakened master. The family not realizing the spells they cast with it are their own Magic(k), because the in-built enchantment got used up long ago.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}